  "notes": [
    "The universe remains degenerate in the ways integration round 2 recorded, and this change closes none of them: the v1 rectangle still cannot make food, and every ruleset comparison taken inside it is still an argument about stone. What this change does close is one wire — mages a universe promotes for itself now join institutions, so scribing runs on the living population instead of on the six mages the scenario founds. That is a mechanism becoming reachable, not a universe becoming balanced.",
    "Capacity is a bound and not a spreading policy. On the founding arm at 600 ticks, 22 living mages sit in one academy of 64 seats while 90 completed universities stand empty -- universityPreference has one answer for the whole universe and there are not enough scholars to fill even one. Spreading is a preference-policy question and belongs to 0.5.0.",
    "NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED and npm run goldens:regen was not run. Measured 2026-08-14 on w116/complete-affiliation merged with origin/main at 0349240. balance-gate-ascension-v1 was deliberately NOT re-recorded: it is the multi-minute gate, it is not required to merge, and CI is the better witness for it."
